    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "I see math as a language of patterns, not just numbers but logic that shapes how I understand the world. It connects with my love for chemistry and literature, offering structure and meaning. Though I’m unemployed, I still explore math through curiosity, especially when it appears in daily life or creative problem-solving.",
    "Do you ever get anxious when thinking about mathematics?": "Yes, sometimes numbers trigger anxiety, especially when I feel unprepared or judged. My high neuroticism makes me overthink mistakes, and low extraversion means I avoid asking for help. But my high conscientiousness pushes me to try again, slowly and carefully, to regain control.",
    "Did you ever use AI to support your math learning in the last year? If yes, how was your experience?": "I haven’t used AI for math recently, but I’ve thought about it. Given my limited access to education and my cautious nature, I’d likely use it sparingly — maybe to check answers or simplify concepts. I’d worry about depending on it, so I’d use it as a tool, not a crutch.",
